---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CableExplorer from '../../components/CableExplorer.jsx';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Cable Explorer" subtitle="Passive spread of voltage along a uniform sealed cable: length constant, steady state and step transients." description="Interactive passive cable: numeric finite-volume solution against the analytic sealed-cable steady state, with length constant and time constants.">
 <nav class="local"><a href="/biology/">Biology</a><a href="/biology/membrane/">Membrane Biophysics</a><a href="/biology/current-clamp/">Current Clamp</a><a href="/cells/">Cell Model Atlas</a><a href="/cortex/?cell=allen-human-571654895%2F1">Cortex Laboratory</a></nav>
 <CableExplorer client:load />
 <section class="panel"><h2>Scope & provenance</h2><table><tbody>
 <tr><th>Model</th><td>Uniform passive cylinder · sealed ends · lateral membrane only · no branches, spines, taper or active channels</td></tr>
 <tr><th>Theory</th><td>Analytic steady state for a finite sealed cable with point current at one end, after Rall · transients are numeric only</td></tr>
 <tr><th>Integration</th><td>Same finite-volume backward-Euler solver as Cortex Laboratory · dt 0.025 ms · 128 compartments · injection held to 6τ</td></tr>
 <tr><th>Comparison</th><td>Numeric steady state shown against the analytic profile live · default parameters agree within 0.5% of V(0)</td></tr>
 <tr><th>Defaults</th><td>Cortex Laboratory passive membrane: Rm 20000 Ω·cm² · Ri 150 Ω·cm · Cm 1 µF/cm² · rest −65 mV</td></tr>
 <tr><th>Interpretation</th><td>A teaching model of passive spread, not a reconstructed neuron · dendrites in the cell atlas carry active mechanisms and branches</td></tr>
 <tr><th>Equations & verification</th><td><a href="/cortex/methods/">Methods</a> · <a href="/cortex/validation/">Numerical verification</a></td></tr>
 </tbody></table></section>
</Layout>
